From 4f398fdbf262f70d5e5d040ddbf65cbbc71253b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: esacademy-de <98397027+esacademy-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:37:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] can: m_can: fix transceiver activation sequencing

The stock open()/close() flow powered the external transceiver on
before m_can_start() configured and started the M_CAN core, which
can expose the CAN bus while the controller's TX behavior is not
yet guaranteed. On some transceivers (e.g. TCAN3413, active-high
STB) that window lets the bus leave standby before the controller
is ready to drive it.

Reorder m_can_open() so phy_power_on() (transceiver standby
deassert) happens only after m_can_start() has successfully put
the controller in Normal Mode, wait out the transceiver's
standby-to-normal transition time (30-50us), and only then start
the TX queue. Unwind in reverse on every failure path: if
phy_power_on() fails after a successful m_can_start(), stop the
M_CAN core again before releasing IRQ/workqueue/NAPI/clock
resources, and never call phy_power_off() for a phy that never
successfully powered on.

m_can_close() already stops the TX queue and the M_CAN core before
asserting transceiver standby, so its order is unchanged.

TODO: Signed-off-by -- add your name and email before submitting
this patch upstream (DCO certification must come from a human
author/maintainer, not be fabricated).
---
 drivers/net/can/m_can/m_can.c | 26 +++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/can/m_can/m_can.c b/drivers/net/can/m_can/m_can.c
index ad4f577c1..8b720b687 100644
--- a/drivers/net/can/m_can/m_can.c
+++ b/drivers/net/can/m_can/m_can.c
@@ -2061,13 +2061,9 @@ static int m_can_open(struct net_device *dev)
 	struct m_can_classdev *cdev = netdev_priv(dev);
 	int err;
 
-	err = phy_power_on(cdev->transceiver);
-	if (err)
-		return err;
-
 	err = m_can_clk_start(cdev);
 	if (err)
-		goto out_phy_power_off;
+		return err;
 
 	/* open the can device */
 	err = open_candev(dev);
@@ -2113,10 +2109,28 @@ static int m_can_open(struct net_device *dev)
 	if (err)
 		goto exit_start_fail;
 
+	/*
+	 * Only now bring the external transceiver out of standby: the
+	 * M_CAN core is configured and already in Normal Mode, so it
+	 * will not drive an undefined bus state once the transceiver
+	 * becomes active. See m_can_close() for the mirrored teardown
+	 * order (stop M_CAN and the queue before re-asserting standby).
+	 */
+	err = phy_power_on(cdev->transceiver);
+	if (err) {
+		netdev_err(dev, "failed to power on can transceiver\n");
+		goto exit_transceiver_fail;
+	}
+
+	/* Wait out the transceiver's standby-to-normal transition time. */
+	usleep_range(30, 50);
+
 	netif_start_queue(dev);
 
 	return 0;
 
+exit_transceiver_fail:
+	m_can_stop(dev);
 exit_start_fail:
 	if (cdev->is_peripheral || dev->irq)
 		free_irq(dev->irq, dev);
@@ -2131,8 +2145,6 @@ out_wq_fail:
 	close_candev(dev);
 exit_disable_clks:
 	m_can_clk_stop(cdev);
-out_phy_power_off:
-	phy_power_off(cdev->transceiver);
 	return err;
 }
 
